# Python testcases and input workbooks

This branch executes native pytest tests for every application. Read
`docs/PYTHON_MIGRATION.md`, the app adapter, and a nearby Python testcase/input
pair before editing. The Excel-driven checkout is a reference, not a runtime
dependency.

## Testcases

- Place executable cases under `Testcases/<APP>/**/test_*.py`, preserving the
  existing feature/tab folders. Use the app's pytest fixture and call adapter
  methods directly. Keep browser behavior in reusable helpers and locators in
  `ObjectRepository/<APP>/`.
- Define suite membership using native `@pytest.mark.quickrun`, `smoke`,
  `regression`, and `datarelease` markers as appropriate. Do not recreate
  `Config/suites.yaml`, Excel Steps, Excel collectors, or Excel action profiles.
- Resolve filter group/value keys from the app's YAML. Preserve action order,
  filters, assertions, report names, and intended coverage when porting a case.
- End comparison cases with the existing framework failure assertion. Functional
  cases need no query workbook unless they actually compare independent data.
- Input/output Excel workbooks remain supported; they are separate from the
  executable Python testcase. Resolve the actual `load_query_file()` argument.

## Query/static input workbooks

- Store expected-data inputs under `InputFiles/<APP>/`. Follow neighboring
  headers (`TabName`, `TabQuery`, `StatQuery`, and supported output-name fields).
  `Commons/query_reader.py` defines the accepted aliases and parser contract.
- Match `TabName` to the adapter's `TabSpec.input_tab` and projected columns to
  the retained UI headers. Stat aliases must match the app's stat names.
- Read `Config/tab_setting.yaml`; sort deterministically before a tab row limit.
  Do not paginate or limit total stat counts. Follow `expected-data.mdc` for all
  SQL/Cypher changes and use static inputs' own existing contracts.
- Preserve established input names, exact capitalization, unrelated cells,
  styles, widths, sheets, dropdowns, and freeze panes. Keep gridlines visible.
  Retain identifiers and leading zeros as text; store readable query text.
- On a rename, update the Python `load_query_file()` call, real input filename,
  output names, and current references. Handle case-only renames safely on macOS.

## Verification

- Collect affected tests; verify fixture, marker, input, method, and locator
  references. Run relevant existing unit checks for shared behavior changes.
- Reopen changed workbooks and validate their contents and parser compatibility.
  Run affected live cases when the environment and expected source are available.
- Inspect matching UI/DB output sheets for failures. Distinguish source drift,
  query defects, scraping defects, and readiness issues. Report unperformed
  checks separately from passes; never weaken comparisons to get a green run.
